    "title": "Nepal-Flooding-Aug-2026",
    "description": "On August 26, 2026, a major flash flood caused by a glacier collapse struck Rasuwa District in northern Nepal after a sudden and intense surge of water entered the Bhote Koshi River from the Tibet (China) side at approximately 9:15 AM local time. The event rapidly affected the border areas of Timure and Rasuwagadhi before moving downstream towards Syabrubesi and the Trishuli River corridor.",
    "license": "CC-BY-NC-4.0",
